+# Crow / field-cipher research recipes — synced 2026-10-02
+
+Six operations were synced into `webxdc/cyberchef/index.html` (441 → 447
+recipes) from the sibling repository `shdwelf/Html5`
+(`public/apps/cyberchef/index.html`), where they were developed during the
+Crow's Cryptogram research passes of 2026-10-02 and are enforced by
+`test/cyberchef-field-museum.test.ts` there. The code is byte-identical apart
+from one inlined helper (`odColumnOrder`, because this build has no
+`deepColumnOrder`).
+
+| Recipe | What it is | Executable control |
+|--------|------------|--------------------|
+| `enigmaM4` | Kriegsmarine four-wheel Enigma: stationary Beta/Gamma Greek wheel + thin B/C reflector. | Beta/A + thin-B ≡ wide UKW-B: `AAAAA → BDZGO`; round-trip with 10 plug pairs. |
+| `secomSchedule` | SECOM key-schedule worksheet (ranks, chain, checkerboard row). | Official worksheet digits `7162830495 / 3728109645 / 0880939030 / 8139065427`. |
+| `odPoemKey` | Dutch Ordedienst poem-code key/indicator worksheet. | Crypto Museum worked example: key `ONZEWASZIENALLE`, indicator `EJHQT`, check `OTRGJ`. |
+| `secomExact` | Full SECOM encrypt/decrypt incl. authoritative triangular disruption. | Reproduces and round-trips the official 105-digit Rijmenants vector; the rejected Crow candidate stays rejected (recorded letter soup). |
+| `iocFitness` | Fitness-ladder instruments: Friedman IoC, Σh² integer IoC, English χ², bigram log-score, Stage-1 calibration rule. | English text scores in the 0.05–0.08 IoC band. |
+| `plugboardHillClimb` | Sullivan–Weierud / Sylichenko plugboard hill-climb over a precomputed step×26 table. | Recovers Stecker `AI EN OS RT` and the full 274-letter plaintext. |
+
+Provenance: the ladder and precompute design follow the published method of
+the Crow's first listed solver, Oleksii Sylichenko
+(<https://github.com/asilichenko/enigma>, LGPL v3). His repository contains
+Enigma tooling only — no SECOM code and no Crow solution — and nothing in
+these recipes reconstructs or implies his private solve. Research notes:
+`docs/lecture-hall-research-2026-10-02.md` and
+`docs/lecture-hall-research-2026-10-02-sylichenko.md` in `shdwelf/Html5`.
+
+CI: `webxdc/cyberchef/recipes-crow.test.mjs` runs all the controls above with
+`node --test` against a stub-DOM sandbox (same pattern as
+`apps/crypto/nsa-enigma.test.mjs`), and the `verify` workflow rebuilds
+`dist/cyberchef.xdc` and requires the committed artifact to match.
